     "text": "I found three problems and fixed all three. I created nothing new and didn't render the drawing to check it afterward.\n\n1. **LN-011:** It sits at the −20 ft offset on T-2, so it is a shoulder edge, but it was on rd_EP. I moved it to rd_ES.\n2. **LN-016:** This is the right (+12) pavement edge on tangent T-2, but it was drawn about 11 ft off the centerline. It also had no alignment anchor. I corrected its endpoints to (2788.53, 1050.2) → (3965.24, 1442.43). I did the arithmetic by hand:\n   - T-2's direction is (0.9487, 0.3162), so the right-hand normal is (0.3162, −0.9487).\n   - The start is the centerline point (2784.74, 1061.58) plus 12 × normal, which gives (2788.53, 1050.20).\n   - The end is the centerline point (3961.44, 1453.81) plus 12 × normal, which gives (3965.24, 1442.43).\n   - It is still unanchored, because modify_entity only changes the geometry.\n3. **EDGE OF PAVEMENT callout:** The leader tip sat at y=980, on the shoulder edge (rd_ES). I moved the leader start LN-017 to y=988, which puts the tip on the pavement edge LN-007. I also moved the arrowhead PL-001 up 8 ft to match.\n\nTool calls, in order:\n- `get_model_state`\n- `modify_entity` LN-011, layer set to rd_ES\n- `modify_entity` LN-016, new start and end as above\n- `modify_entity` LN-017, start set to [1702.633, 988]\n- `move_entities` PL-001, delta [0, 8]\n\nThe only failure was my first call, `get_document_state`, which returned \"No such tool available\". I used `get_model_state` instead and had no other problems."
